-- title:
--   Local conductor–discriminant formula for an induced character
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` which is a number field and Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, write $G = F \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} F$ for its automorphism group, let $H \le G$ be a subgroup and $\chi : H \to \mathbb{C}^{\times}$ a group homomorphism. Let $p$ be a prime number and let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_F$ whose contraction to $\mathbb{Z}$ is the ideal generated by $p$. For $j \in \mathbb{N}$ put $G_j = (\mathfrak{P}^{j+1})$`.inertia`$\,G$, the $j$-th lower ramification group, so $G_0$ is the inertia group attached to $\mathfrak{P}^1$. The assertion is an identity in $\mathbb{C}$: the finite sum over $j \in \mathbb{N}$ of $$\frac{|G_j|}{|G_0|}\Bigl(\,[G:H] \;-\; \frac{1}{|G_j|}\sum_{g \in G_j} \varphi(g)\Bigr), \qquad \varphi(g) = \frac{1}{|H|}\sum_{x \in G} \begin{cases} \chi(x^{-1} g x) & x^{-1} g x \in H\\ 0 & \text{otherwise,}\end{cases}$$ equals the exponent of $p$ in the factorisation of the natural number $|\mathrm{discr}(K)| \cdot N(\mathfrak{f})$, cast into $\mathbb{C}$. Here $K$ is the fixed field of $H$, $N$ is the absolute ideal norm, and $\mathfrak{f} \subseteq \mathcal{O}_K$ is $\prod_v v^{a_v}$ over the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_K$, with $a_v = (1$ unless the character is unramified at $v$, in which case $0) + \lceil$ its Swan conductor at $v \rceil$, the character being $\chi$ transported to $F \simeq_K F$ along the canonical isomorphism of that group with $H$.
--
--   This is the prime-by-prime (local) form of the conductor–discriminant formula for the character induced from a one-dimensional character $\chi$ of a subgroup $H$: the left-hand side is the Artin conductor exponent at $p$ of $\mathrm{Ind}_H^G \chi$, computed through the lower ramification filtration at a prime $\mathfrak{P}$ above $p$, and the right-hand side is the exponent of $p$ in $|d_K| \cdot N_{K/\mathbb{Q}} \mathfrak{f}(\chi)$ for $K = F^H$. It feeds into [`ArtinL.conductor_mul_prod_pow_eq_prod_pow_of_trace_eq_sum`](thm.html#ArtinL.conductor_mul_prod_pow_eq_prod_pow_of_trace_eq_sum), which assembles conductors of Artin representations from induced characters.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ArtinL_finsum_card_mul_sub_sum_induced_eq_factorization_discr_mul_absNorm_conductor.lean

